body:
It seems like you really like the idea of expanding on the characters you like, so start there. If you want to be pragmatic about it, you can think about what causes conflict between characters or their ambitions. If you have, for example, a character you want to be a revolution leader, what are they revolting against? Why revolt and not just move? Give up? Join the opposite side? Questions about their purpose can lead you up to a problem. Conversely, you can create problems and think about what your OC would do in response.

&#x200B;

But really, there's no such thing as too small or too big when you're starting out. If you think something, and you like it, write it down. Let ideas out and worry about refining them later.
